<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>NUSX Plaud Team Sync — Privacy Policy</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/mascot.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <img class="logo" src="/nusx-logo.svg" alt="NUSX" width="120" height="38" />
      <h1>NUSX Plaud Team Sync — Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>

      <p>
        NUSX Plaud Team Sync is a Chrome extension for NUSX staff. It copies your own Plaud recordings into the
        Team files of your NUSX Plaud Team workspace.
      </p>

      <h2>What it handles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Plaud sign-in data.</strong> The Plaud workspace token and refresh token that Plaud Web issues to
          you, your Plaud API region and your current workspace ID. It reads the Plaud sign-in cookie
          (<code>pld_ut</code>) on <code>plaud.ai</code> to renew access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Recording metadata.</strong> The list of your Plaud recordings: IDs, names, start times,
          durations and whether each has a transcript. The extension does not download or read the audio,
          transcripts or summaries.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Its own settings and history.</strong> The team workspace and folder you chose, sync options, and
          which recordings it has already shared or asked Plaud to transcribe.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What it does with it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Lists your recordings, asks Plaud to transcribe the ones without a transcript, and shares eligible
          recordings into your team's Team files, using Plaud's own API on your behalf.
        </li>
        <li>All of this data stays in <code>chrome.storage.local</code> in your Chrome profile.</li>
        <li>
          It is sent only to Plaud (<code>*.plaud.ai</code>), over HTTPS. It is not sent to NUSX, the developer, or
          any other third party, and there is no analytics or tracking.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The extension does not sell or transfer your data, and does not use it for any purpose other than the
          single purpose above.
        </li>
        <li>
          Recordings it shares become visible to all members of your Plaud Team workspace, as with sharing from
          Plaud Web. Plaud's own privacy policy governs data held by Plaud.
        </li>
        <li>Removing the extension deletes everything it stored in your browser.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>NUSX AI &amp; Systems, <a href="mailto:song.luar@nus.edu.sg">song.luar@nus.edu.sg</a>.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

